#
# Deployed and measured 2026-09-02 against production:
#
#   UPPERCASE request  /locations/%D7%A9%D7%9B...%9C/   -> 301 -> /%D7%90%D7%96...%AA/   ✅ rule fires
#   lowercase request  /locations/%d7%a9%d7%9b...%9c/   -> 404                            ❌ no match
#
# Cloudflare Pages UPPERCASE-NORMALISES the source path of a rule at parse time, then matches it
# against the RAW request path. This site emits LOWERCASE %d7% everywhere — sitemap.xml, every
# canonical, every authored href — so every real, indexed URL is lowercase and can never match a
# rule. Writing the rule in lowercase does not help: it is normalised to uppercase too. Raw
# unencoded Hebrew does not help: dalita.co.il proves it normalises to uppercase as well.
#
# THE ASYMMETRY THAT HIDES THIS: static ASSET lookup IS case-insensitive — both cases of a live
# page return 200 — while RULE matching is case-sensitive. So poking a live URL by hand tells you
# nothing about whether a rule would match, and a reviewer who tests only assets concludes the
# opposite of the truth. I made exactly that error on the first pass.
#
# CONSEQUENCE: the seven withdrawn location pages return 404 on the form Google indexed. The
# rules below still earn their place — they catch uppercase-encoded backlinks and crawlers — but
# they are a partial mitigation, not the fix.
#
# THE ACTUAL FIX IS A ZONE-LEVEL REDIRECT RULE (owner action — CLAUDE.md §13 says Cloudflare zone
# settings are the owner's to change). Dashboard → the 3locksmiths.co.il zone → Rules → Redirect
# Rules → Create. Use a lower() transform so BOTH cases match:
#
#   When incoming requests match:
#     lower(http.request.uri.path) in {
#       "/locations/%d7%a9%d7%9b%d7%a4%d7%95%d7%9c-%d7%9e%d7%a4%d7%aa%d7%97-%d7%91%d7%90%d7%a8-%d7%a9%d7%91%d7%a2/"
#       "/locations/%d7%a9%d7%9b%d7%a4%d7%95%d7%9c-%d7%9e%d7%a4%d7%aa%d7%97-%d7%91%d7%99%d7%a8%d7%95%d7%a9%d7%9c%d7%99%d7%9d/"
#       "/locations/%d7%a9%d7%9b%d7%a4%d7%95%d7%9c-%d7%9e%d7%a4%d7%aa%d7%97-%d7%91%d7%99%d7%aa-%d7%a9%d7%9e%d7%a9/"
#       "/locations/%d7%a9%d7%9b%d7%a4%d7%95%d7%9c-%d7%9e%d7%a4%d7%aa%d7%97-%d7%90%d7%a9%d7%a7%d7%9c%d7%95%d7%9f/"
#       "/locations/%d7%a9%d7%9b%d7%a4%d7%95%d7%9c-%d7%9e%d7%a4%d7%aa%d7%97-%d7%9b%d7%a8%d7%9e%d7%99%d7%90%d7%9c/"
#       "/locations/%d7%a9%d7%9b%d7%a4%d7%95%d7%9c-%d7%9e%d7%a4%d7%aa%d7%97-%d7%a2%d7%9b%d7%95/"
#       "/locations/%d7%a9%d7%9b%d7%a4%d7%95%d7%9c-%d7%9e%d7%a4%d7%aa%d7%97-%d7%a2%d7%a4%d7%95%d7%9c%d7%94/"
#     }
#   Then: Static redirect → /%d7%90%d7%96%d7%95%d7%a8%d7%99-%d7%a9%d7%99%d7%a8%d7%95%d7%aa/ , 301
#
# ⚠️ FLEET-WIDE: every sibling site with Hebrew slugs has the same latent defect. galbath.co.il's
# uppercase rules only catch uppercase traffic; dalita.co.il's raw-Hebrew rules likewise. None of
# them redirect the lowercase URLs their own sitemaps publish.
#
# Ships in out/ from public/ (next build copies public/ wholesale). wrangler auto-detects it —
# ops/deploy-site.ps1 does not special-case it; line 255 is a plain `npx wrangler pages deploy`.
# Format: <from>  <to>  <status>. First match wins.
#
# NO WILDCARDS UNDER /locations/. _redirects outranks existing static assets on Pages, and a
# `/locations/*` catch-all cannot be fenced off — the per-survivor rules that would protect the
# 25 live city pages get uppercase-normalised too, so lowercase survivor traffic would fall
# through the fence and be redirected away. Exact paths only.
#
